  "component_decisions": [
    {
      "component": "Finite↔Nat prediction connection",
      "body_count": 5,
      "approved": true,
      "scope": "Both finite state/input coordinate recoveries, actual all-stage dynamics/row/terminal conversion in both directions, feasible-domain equivalence and firstinput equality. The zero extension after the horizon supplies no later constraint; the terminal extension constructor supplies those separately. N=0 conversion is valid; firstinput requires genuine N>0."
    },
    {
      "component": "Attained original global MPC and robust certificate",
      "body_count": 2,
      "approved": true,
      "scope": "Total classical firstinput policy is chosen from previously derived compact attained global optimizers, with zero off the feasible domain. The robust theorem uses an actual old feasible prediction/firstinput choice and the approved source-assumption bootstrap to construct every new original constraint and derive actual U membership. It supplies no desired successor-X or next-feasibility premise. Optimality is derived by the separate first body, not required for the bootstrap; classical choice supplies no measurability."
    },
    {
      "component": "Terminal invariance→actual original feasibility",
      "body_count": 2,
      "approved": true,
      "scope": "Genuine terminal-control recursion is inducted inside the terminal set. Terminal rows at N and monotonic epsilon imply every earlier row; dynamics, initial and final membership are constructed. Includes N=0. hinvariant is the source local terminal ingredient, not whole recursive MPC feasibility."
    },
    {
      "component": "Actual epsilon, domain rows, sublevel and safety projection",
      "body_count": 5,
      "approved": true,
      "scope": "Nonnegative coefficient and geometric increments give nonnegative/monotone epsilon, even without epsilonN≤1. True terminal rows imply X/U. Continuous sublevel is closed/compact conditional on explicit sublevel⊆compact X; that inclusion is to be instantiated from the preceding row lemma. Feasibility⊆X derives from stage0 and epsilon0=0 with N>0. Final safety/convergence projection takes an already obtained actual outcome and feasible⊆X; it is a projection component, not a derivation of the whole outcome."
    },
    {
      "component": "Physical infinity-input quadratic cost",
      "body_count": 4,
      "approved": true,
      "scope": "WithLp.toLp2 preserves every input coordinate; finite-dimensional continuity transports the actual Pi-infinity physical input into the selected Euclidean matrix quadratic. Genuine stage/terminal continuity and positive-definite input-cost nonnegativity follow. No norm equivalence is silently substituted in the robust error bound."
    }
  ],
